WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
Exam day.

2
00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.910
The desk is bare: no
books allowed in the room.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.370
The paper offers four questions.

4
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:11.200
Two works you've studied
float in your head, closed.

5
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.770
One by one the questions light up.

6
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.470
The books glow green, then grey.

7
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.310
Fits?

8
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.390
Doesn't fit?

9
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.190
Four questions, one
choice, nothing to look at.

10
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.870
So how do you choose?

11
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.190
In this mission, you'll
see what Paper 2 asks:

12
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.610
comparing and contrasting
two works you have studied.

13
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.870
You'll ask what really makes one
question easier to answer than another.

14
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.670
And you'll see two ways
to build the essay:

15
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.980
in blocks, or integrated
all the way through.

16
00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:44.350
Your mission: work out how
to choose your question.
